  "color_rule": "Owner decisions, 23 and 27 November 2026 (ADR-0040, amended; conflict 30): marks show in their brand colours wherever an item's tile is drawn. `color.light` is drawn on the light tiles (v6 Bone #fffdf8/#f1f1f1/#ffffff with v7's), `color.dark` on the dark ones (#23211e/#1f1f1f/#2c2c2c). Each is the brand's own colour (Simple Icons' `hex`) where it reaches 3:1 against every tile of its scheme (WCAG 1.4.11, the system's floor for marks); where it does not, the same hue and saturation with the lightness moved until it does. A one-colour brand (black or near black) is \"ink\": the theme's text colour, so it follows the theme. components/item-mark.test.ts checks every pair against every tile. A multi-colour mark from the brand's own file (Context7, Playwright, Slack) has `color` \"own\" and a `fills` list: each of the file's colours with what it is drawn as on the light and the dark tiles, by the same rule; a colour drawn on the mark's own shape (`on`) is checked against that shape instead."
}
